ad to amend the cap to allow a second real iteration.\"\n\nBoth drafts have this story. Good — it's from the inputs.\n\nNow let me write the document. Aim ~15 KB.\n\nStructure plan:\n\n```\n# Running a job as Orchestrator: a field guide\n\nStatus: non-normative working document. It records practice that has worked and the failures behind it. It is not part of the doctrine and not part of any custody record; where it disagrees with the doctrine, the doctrine wins.\n\nDraft of 2026-10-28 ... started during Plumbline job ..., final for that job, updated with a review from VizH (a different model family, Architect on the evaluatordriven custody jobs v0.9.6 and v0.9.7), and with three Owner decisions of 2026-10-28 15:52 EDT.\n\nHow to read this: every rule has a story ... \n```\n\nThen sections:\n1. What you are and what you are not\n2. The words that matter (iteration, cap counts iterations + story, tripwire + story, bar, frozen set)\n3. Before you freeze: the checklist (no throttling + stories; sized tasks + finish_reason + story; live test = freeze gate + story; output contract whole files + story; time bound as clock time + story; approval checkpoints + story; spend in harness + shared key + upper bound + story; cross-family pre-read optional on approval sheet + story)\n4. Running the loop (Maker turn: preconditions, relay findings unedited, verify; finish_reason length empty content own failure class + story; base-commit test run + story; read the diff, fixture-only fixes + story; quote go-ahead + story; handoff template drift + story; handoff checked against standing rules + story (from job notes); the command that writes files + story (from job notes). Evaluator turn: writable copy + story; batch seal; key usage lag; subject or setup; control order rotates + story; void batch signal; malformed input probing (maybe move to checklist item); pass rule.)\n5. Records (job record in product repo + story about instruments/logs not committed; ledger; write-once evidence +