o: the cap rule gets the story; the \"write the cap in one sentence\" item can say \"the same incident: ...\" and refer back.\n\nLet me write:\n\n**2.2 The cap counts iterations**\n- Rule: The cap counts E-DI iterations — one Maker produce, one Evaluator score, one pass-rule application. Maker-internal attempts (retries, follow-ups, regenerations inside one turn) are not iterations.\n- *Story:* bar said \"cap 3 generations\"; gens 1-2 died on plumbing (token cap, malformed diffs) before any scoring; iteration 1 failed scoring and the bar said the attempts were gone; the Owner had to amend the cap to allow a second real iteration.\n- Then a follow-on item: write the cap in one sentence, \"cap N E-DI iterations; Maker attempts limited by budget, the clock-time bound, and the repeat-failure tripwire.\" with a note: the story is the one above; also VizH's jobs hit the same thing with \"3 revisions\" counting sessions and round-trips.\n\nGood.\n\nNow let me draft the whole thing carefully.\n\nAlso need: \"finish_reason\" appears with \"length\" and \"empty content\" and \"own failure class\" — one place: \"Treat `finish_reason` `length` with empty content as its own failure class: stop at the first one, resize the request, and do not retry it as is.\"\n\nCareful: normalization drops backticks, so `finish_reason` → finish_reason (underscore dropped → \"finishreason\"). Wait! The normalize rule: \"drop the characters * _ ` and backslash\". So `finish_reason` becomes \"finishreason\"! Then the anchor \"finish_reason\" would NOT match!! Hmm. The anchor list says C1 needs \"finish_reason\". If underscores are dropped from the text, then \"finish_reason\" in the anchor must also be normalized the same way... The evaluator presumably normalizes both the text and the anchors the same way, so anchor \"finish_reason\" → \"finishreason\" and my text \"finish_reason\" → \"finishreason\" matches. Yes — normalization applied to both sides. So it's fine either way. But to be safe, does