            "role": "user",
            "content": "# Part `guide` (6 of 6): checks G4-G7, J3 and J4: the new Orchestrator field guide (approval item 30)\n\nThe commission is the frozen bar below (custody/bar.md, sha256 72e92dc7580e2447f19dfff66aaac02d8484157a6283dcfdda6c7bb2de7561c6). This request covers only the part named above; the parts, in order, are `ledger`, `emitter`, `verifier`, `edi`, `docs`, `guide`. Allowed paths for this part: docs/PLUMBLINE-ORCHESTRATOR-FIELD-GUIDE.md (new; the only file of this request).\n\n## Frozen bar: allow-list (verbatim)\n\n## Allow-list (spec)\n- **Edit:** `kit/custody_ledger.py`, `kit/emit_custody.py`, `kit/custody_history.py`, `kit/plumbline_job.py` (only to pass `--allow-hand-times` through to the emitter at close, and to run the verifier at close and refuse on failure; V8), `tests/validate_schemas.py`, `docs/custody-emission.md`, `kit/README.md`.\n- **New files only:**\n  - `tools/edi/**`;\n  - `kit/plumbline_verify.py` (V1–V9);\n  - `docs/PLUMBLINE-ORCHESTRATOR-FIELD-GUIDE.md` (item 30; the only file for that item);\n  - `schemas/x-plumbline/x-plumbline-v1.schema.json` (the only new file allowed under `schemas/`);\n  - `tests/test_edi_*.py`, `tests/test_custody_ledger*.py`, `tests/test_plumbline_verify*.py`;\n  - new folders under `tests/fixtures/custody/` (new planted or clean cases).\n- **Unchanged, byte for byte:**\n  - every file under `tests/fixtures/` at 3df1ce5;\n  - everything under `dot-plumbline/jobs/`;\n  - every file under `schemas/` at 3df1ce5 (15 files; derived or vendored, pinned by `tools/pin.json`), plus `gate/` and `standards/`;\n  - `tools/pin.json` and `tools/build_schemas.py`.\n- **Fixture-only and test-only fixes are not acceptable** (approval item 16). A fixture or test change never counts as the fix for a finding. The Orchestrator names the kind of fix in each generation-close line.\n\n## Frozen bar: Maker output contract (verbatim)\n\n## Maker output contract\n- Whole files, between `<<<PLUMBLINE-FILE path=<path>>>>` / `<<<PLUMBLINE-END path=<path>>>>` markers, ending with `<<<PLUMBLINE-DONE files=N>>>` (job 1's format; `handoffs/extract_files.py`, which also limits each request to its part's paths). No diffs.\n- An iteration may take several Maker calls, for example one per part. The iteration's revision is the single commit made from all of them.\n- **The field guide is its own Maker request** (item 30), separate from every code-file request, so no single request risks `finish_reason` `length`. It counts under the same money bound, clock-time bound and cap.\n- The runbook names the command that writes the files (`extract_files.py` **without** `--check`) before the commit.\n- Commits: author `E-DI Maker`, committer `Steve Moitozo II <smoitozo@users.noreply.github.com>`.\n\n## What to write\n\nWrite ONE new file, `docs/PLUMBLINE-ORCHESTRATOR-FIELD-GUIDE.md`: the Plumbline Orchestrator field guide. Merge the two drafts below into one document: the Owner's draft gives the base structure and the generic \"Owner\" voice; the Orchestrator's guide gives the newer content. Requirements (approval item 30):\n(a) a status line near the top: the document is non-normative and the doctrine wins on conflict;\n(b) it reflects the Owner decisions of 2026-10-28 15:52 EDT: the tripwire at exactly 3 of the same failure class, then change the request; the shared key behind the harness pre-call spend guard, with key-usage reconciliation called an upper bound (do not recommend a per-job key); the cross-family pre-read optional, decided per job on the approval sheet;\n(c) it keeps these rules: finish_reason length with empty content is its own failure class (stop at the first one); no throttling (endpoint max output, no reasoning limit), sized tasks, finish_reason logged on every call; the cap counts E-DI iterations; handoffs name the command that writes files; check handoffs against standing rules; a live test of each model instrument is a freeze gate; write-once evidence; relayed approvals are not approval